{"name":"Caraway Shield","hex":"#ab9975","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caraway","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A biennial plant of species Carum carvi, native to Europe and Asia, mainly grown for its seed to be used as a culinary spice.","The seed-like fruit of the caraway plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caraway"},{"term":"shield","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Anything that protects or defends; defense; shelter; protection.\nA broad piece of defensive armor, held in hand, formerly in general use in war, for the protection of the body.\n\n One who protects or defends.\n\n A featherless, flat, fleshy protuberance on the head; a frontal shield.\n A flattish patch of iridescent feathers.\n A heavily hardened, protective plate on an insect's exoskeleton that covers part of its body.\n In lichens, a hardened cup or disk surrounded by a rim and containing the fructification, or asci.\n A framework used to protect workmen in making an adit under ground, and capable of being pushed along as excavation progresses.\n\n A field of energy that protects or defends.","A broad piece of defensive armor, held in hand, formerly in general use in war, for the protection of the body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To protect, to defend.","To shelter; to protect oneself."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shield"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caraway","blocks":[{"text":"Caraway, also known as meridian fennel, is a biennial plant in the family Apiaceae, native to western Asia, Europe, and North Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Carum_carvi_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-172.jpg/330px-Carum_carvi_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-172.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caraway"},{"title":"Shield","blocks":[{"text":"A shield is a piece of personal armour held in the hand, which may or may not be strapped to the wrist or forearm. Shields are used to intercept specific attacks, whether from close-ranged weaponry like spears or long ranged projectiles such as arrows. They function as means of active blocks, as well as to provide passive protection by closing one or more lines of engagement during combat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/The_uncivilized_races_of_men_in_all_countries_of_the_world%3B_being_a_comprehensive_account_of_their_manners_and_customs%2C_and_of_their_physical%2C_social%2C_mental%2C_moral_and_religious_characteristics._By_%2814762645001%29.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shield"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/K%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg/500px-K%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/K%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg/1280px-K%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/K%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg/500px-K%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caraway fruits, informally called \"seeds\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AK%C3%BCmmel_2012-07-08-9523.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/NAMA_Myc%C3%A8nes_bouclier_1.jpg/500px-NAMA_Myc%C3%A8nes_bouclier_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/NAMA_Myc%C3%A8nes_bouclier_1.jpg/500px-NAMA_Myc%C3%A8nes_bouclier_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wall painting depicting a My